cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Se usar o trama, cite-o com os metadados abaixo."
type: software
title: "trama: Interactive Node-Graph Computation with Live Previews"
version: 0.5.3
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/uaipedro/trama"
url: "https://github.com/uaipedro/trama"
authors:
  - given-names: Pedro
    family-names: Mambelli Fernandes
    email: pedromambelli@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-1695-279X"
  - given-names: João Paulo Assis
    family-names: Bonifácio
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-2335-8391"
abstract: >-
  Build and run computation graphs interactively. Nodes are typed R functions
  with declared ports and parameters; a flow is a plain JSON document;
  execution is pull-based, content-addressed and incremental. Domain knowledge
  lives entirely in registrable collections, never in the core.
keywords:
  - R
  - shiny
  - visual programming
  - statistics
